1
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Be careful what you wish for.

2
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:26,000
Coraline is a animation, family, fantasy film directed by Henry Selick.

3
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Wandering her rambling old house in her boring new town, 11-year-old Coraline
discovers a hidden door to a strangely idealized version of her life.

4
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:46,000
In order to stay in the fantasy, she must make a frighteningly real sacrifice.

5
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:56,000
Coraline Jones (voice), played by Dakota Fanning.

6
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:06,000
Mel Jones / Other Mother (voice), played by Teri Hatcher.

7
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:16,000
Miss April Spink / Other Spink (voice), played by Jennifer Saunders.

8
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:26,000
Miss Miriam Forcible / Other Forcible (voice), played by Dawn French.

9
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:36,000
The Cat (voice), played by Keith David.

10
00:41:40,000 --> 00:41:46,000
Charlie Jones / Other Father (voice), played by John Hodgman.

11
00:45:50,000 --> 00:45:56,000
Coraline is a 2009 American stop-motion animated dark fantasy horror film written and
directed by Henry Selick, based on the 2002 novella by Neil Gaiman.

12
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
The first feature film produced by Laika Studios, it features the voices of Dakota
Fanning, Teri Hatcher, Jennifer Saunders, Dawn French, and Ian McShane.

13
00:54:10,000 --> 00:54:16,000
The film tells the story of a young girl discovering an idealized alternate universe behind a
secret door in her new home, unaware that it contains something dark and sinister.

14
00:58:20,000 --> 00:58:26,000
As Gaiman was finishing his novella, he met Selick and invited him to make a film
adaptation, as Gaiman was a fan of Selick's other stop-motion works.

15
01:02:30,000 --> 01:02:36,000
When Selick thought that a direct adaptation would lead to
"maybe a 47-minute movie", the story was expanded.

16
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
Looking for a design different from that of most animation, Selick discovered the work of
Japanese illustrator Tadahiro Uesugi and invited him to become the concept artist.

17
01:10:50,000 --> 01:10:56,000
Uesugi's biggest influences were on the color palette, which was muted in
the real world and more colorful in the alternate universe.

18
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
Production of the animation took place at a warehouse in Hillsboro, Oregon.

19
01:19:10,000 --> 01:19:16,000
Coraline premiered at the Portland International Film Festival on February 5, 2009, and was
released theatrically in the United States on February 6 by Focus Features.

20
01:23:20,000 --> 01:23:26,000
The film was met with widespread acclaim from critics and
grossed $126 million on its initial release.

21
01:27:30,000 --> 01:27:36,000
Several theatrical re-releases raised its box office total to $186 million,
making it the third-highest-grossing stop-motion film of all time.

22
01:31:40,000 --> 01:31:46,000
The film won Annie Awards for Best Music, Best Character Design, and Best Production Design, and
was nominated for Best Animated Feature at the Academy Awards and the Golden Globes.

23
01:35:50,000 --> 01:35:56,000
The film explores themes of friendship, dreams,
based on novel or book, villain, eye.
